INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Benchmark sources on Ronin and Harmony Horizon thefts", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003; SRC-004", "text": "SRC-003 (Elliptic) reports the March 2022 Ronin theft: 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC, worth $540m at theft; OFAC on Apr 14 2022 sanctioned the thief Ethereum address and identified its owner as Lazarus Group, a North Korean state hacking group. Elliptic says stolen USDC was swapped for ETH through DEXs, then $16.7m ETH moved through three centralized exchanges, and after exchanges announced cooperation with law enforcement the attacker used Tornado Cash; $80.3m ETH had gone through Tornado Cash and $9.7m was in intermediary wallets, with $433m remaining in the original wallet as of Apr 14. Ronin's postmortem said five of nine validator private keys were obtained and evidence pointed to social engineering. SRC-002 (Chainalysis) says Lazarus accessed five of nine Ronin validator keys and approved withdrawals of 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC; laundering used over 12,000 addresses and a typical North Korean pattern: intermediary wallets, Tornado Cash mixing, ETH-to-BTC swaps, Bitcoin mixing, and crypto-to-fiat cashout. It also describes chain-hopping across Ethereum, BNB and BitTorrent and reports over $30m seized, approximately 10% of stolen funds, while much remained in wallets. SRC-001 (Elliptic) states the FBI confirmed Lazarus, backed by North Korea, behind the June 24 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge theft of $99.7m. It says Elliptic identified similarities with Lazarus blockchain laundering patterns; Horizon funds were programmatically structured through Tornado Cash, mirroring Ronin laundering. Elliptic estimates over $555m sent through Tornado Cash from the two hacks: over $468m Ronin and $96m Harmony. After Tornado Cash sanctions, funds were structured through Railgun; about 70% of funds sent through Railgun were estimated to be Harmony funds. Post-Railgun funds went to three exchanges; Binance and Huobi said they identified, blocked and seized part. SRC-004 contains no substantive case facts beyond a generic Elliptic research listing. No source returned explicit APT38 identification or specific wallet addresses."}
